  "data": {
    "accession": "PXD040902",
    "title": "Determination of protein monoclonal-antibody epitopes by a combination of  structural proteomics methods.",
    "additionalAttributes": [],
    "projectDescription": "We use a combination of multiple structural proteomics techniques (differential photo-reactive surface modification, HDX, crosslinking and epitope excision/extraction) for the determination of the protein antigen epitopes for monoclonal antibodies.",
    "sampleProcessingProtocol": "Free protein antigen (p24) and antigen-antibody (p24-MabE) complexes (Grifols) were crosslinked with the hetero-bifunctional crosslinking reagent SDA (Thermo).  Antigen-antibody complexes were crosslinked with DSS long-distance crosslinking reagent (Creative Molecules).The crosslinked proteins were enzymatically digested with trypsin and the resulting digests were analyzed by LC-MS using an Orbitrap QE+ mass spectrometer (Thermo).  Photo-reactive surface modification data were extracted from the crosslinking datasets as dead-end modifications with hydrolyzed SDA reagent or intra-peptide SDA crosslinks.",
    "dataProcessingProtocol": "Differentially modified residues were determined using label free quantitation analysis with Proteome Discoverer (Thermo).  Crosslinked residues were identified using XlinkX node of the Proteome Discoverer and DXMSMS Match.  Epitope extraction/excision was performed using MabE antibodies immobilized on Dynabeads M-270 Epoxy (Thermo).  Intact protein and bottom-up differential hydrogen-deuterium exchange analysis (HDX) was performed by using LC-MS on a TripleTOF 6600 mass spectrometer (Sciex), data were processed using MS Studio.",
    "projectTags": [],
    "keywords": [
      "Hdx",
      "Limited proteolysis",
